meta {
  name: process image upload
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{SUPABASE_URL}}/functions/v1/process-image-upload
  body: multipartForm
  auth: none
}

headers {
  apikey: {{SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY}}
  Authorization: Bearer {{SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  file: @file({{IMAGE_FILE_PATH}})
  target: profile_header
  ~crop: {"x":0,"y":250,"width":1000,"height":375}
  ~destination: headers
}

docs {
  Send a JPEG, PNG or WebP source using IMAGE_FILE_PATH and an authenticated user token.
  Optional crop and destination rows are disabled by default; enable crop after choosing
  coordinates that fit your source. Do not set Content-Type manually: Bruno supplies
  the multipart boundary. This is an Edge Function, so PostgREST schema headers do not apply.

  crop is one JSON text field with exactly x, y, width and height as safe integers.
  Coordinates use the original image AFTER EXIF orientation, from its top-left before
  resizing. x/y must be non-negative; width/height positive; the rectangle must be wholly
  inside the source. The example selects a 1000x375 strip from a 1000x1000 source.
  Use source pixels, not CSS preview pixels. The field is limited to 256 characters.

  Processing auto-orients and crops first, then applies the configured target without
  upscaling. inside retains the selected ratio; cover may centre-crop again to its
  configured ratio. Omitting crop preserves previous behaviour. The target remains
  authoritative for output dimensions, format, quality, bucket, filename and visibility.
  destination optionally selects a safe relative directory beneath the authenticated
  user's ID. It cannot contain absolute paths, unsafe segments, leading/trailing slashes,
  or more than 256 characters. Storage uses the caller's RLS, never a service-role client.

  Core starter targets: profile_avatar (300x300 maximum) and profile_header (1600x600
  maximum), JPEG quality 80, private user-avatars bucket, one-hour signed URL. Consumers
  retain their own target maps and document product targets separately. Source limits
  apply before cropping: starter limits are 5 MiB and 25 megapixels.

  200: target, bucket, path, content_type, width, height, bytes, plus configured signed_url
  and signed_url_expires_in or public_url. No crop is echoed. Persist path for profile images.
  400: malformed/unknown/duplicate/missing multipart fields, unsupported target, unsafe
  destination, malformed crop JSON or invalid crop shape/types. 401: missing/invalid user
  JWT. 405: unsupported method. 413: source byte limit. 415: unsupported declared/decoded
  image type. 422: decode/pixel-limit failure or crop outside the oriented source.
  500: Storage or signed-URL failure. Deploy the updated function before sending crop.
}
